WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.920
In the aftermath of the Battle of Winterfell,
beyond the thousands of men left dead and

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:09.270
injured, allegiances have shifted, alliances
have changed, and, of course, there's still

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:10.750
another war to fight.

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:15.099
Cersei is still waiting, and her army is ready
to attack Daenerys, Jon, and their allied

00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:16.099
forces.

00:00:16.099 --> 00:00:19.759
With just a handful of episodes remaining
in the final season, there's plenty left to

00:00:19.759 --> 00:00:24.039
accomplish, between the quest for the throne
as well as another war, so here's everything

00:00:24.039 --> 00:00:28.659
you need to know about "The Last of the Starks,"
the fourth episode of the last season of Game

00:00:28.659 --> 00:00:29.659
of Thrones.

00:00:29.659 --> 00:00:30.689
Funerals, celebrations, &amp; proposals

00:00:30.689 --> 00:00:34.809
As you might expect after the carnage of the
Battle of Winterfell, "The Last of the Starks"

00:00:34.809 --> 00:00:37.820
opens with a slow and emotional funeral sequence.

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:41.230
Characters like Daenerys and Sansa are given
the chance to mourn loved ones, including

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:45.140
Jorah Mormont and Theon Greyjoy, who gave
their lives during the battle.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:49.339
After a moving speech by Jon, the entire crew
retires to the great hall of Winterfell to

00:00:49.339 --> 00:00:53.350
celebrate their victory, giving the characters
as well as the audience a brief respite from

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:54.969
the violence and sadness.

00:00:54.969 --> 00:00:58.809
During the celebration, Daenerys takes a moment
to win some more brownie points with the Northerners

00:00:58.809 --> 00:01:03.749
by naming Gendry, Robert Baratheon's illegitimate
son and sole remaining heir, as the Lord of

00:01:03.749 --> 00:01:04.830
Storm's End.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:09.150
Encouraged by his new title and still stuck
on his one night with Arya, Gendry rushes

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:13.440
off to propose to his lady love, only to be
gently yet firmly rebuffed.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:17.810
Arya definitely isn't looking to get wifed
up any time soon, and being the lady of a

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:22.590
grand castle probably isn't quite as appealing
as stealing faces and killing enemies.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:26.740
So unfortunately for Gendry, he'll probably
have to find a different lady to help run

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:27.740
his castle.

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:31.610
At this point, it's looking like Robert's
dream of joining the Baratheon and Stark houses

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:33.490
may not come true after all.

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:34.670
Brienne loves… and loses

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:38.220
Ever since she traveled with the Kingslayer
several seasons ago and saw his fall from

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:43.200
celebrated knight to one-handed enemy of Queen
Cersei, Brienne has clearly had feelings for

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.200
Jaime.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.340
And it certainly seemed as if he returned
those feelings, from the time he saved her

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:51.820
from a bear pit to the moment he dubbed her
the first female Knight of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:56.240
After Tyrion shrewdly reveals that Brienne
is a virgin during a drinking game, the formidable

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.840
fighter is uncharacteristically embarrassed.

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:02.480
But once Jaime comes to comfort her, she gets
over that embarrassment pretty quickly.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:05.700
Jaime, however, has to choose where his allegiances
lie.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:10.000
Despite his seemingly close relationships
with both Tyrion and Brienne, he ends up heading

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.220
right back to Cersei.

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:14.920
As he leaves in the middle of the night, Brienne
rushes to bring him back to the Northern side,

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:19.120
but he insists he's really just as "hateful"
as his sister and leaves her heartbroken.

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:24.000
A Lannister always pays his debts, but which
scores will Jaime be hoping to settle when

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.500
he gets back to King's Landing?

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:26.740
News travels fast

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:31.090
The news that Jon Snow isn't Ned Stark's bastard
at all, but the legitimate son of Prince Rhaegar

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:35.900
Targaryen and Ned's sister Lyanna, has been
out in the open for viewers since season 7,

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:39.590
when Bran and Sam discovered the truth about
his secret royal lineage.

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:43.620
As the person with the strongest claim to
the Iron Throne, Jon has unwittingly made

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:48.350
himself an enemy of just about everyone on
the show, especially his new girlfriend Daenerys,

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:52.160
who is also his aunt, in case all of this
needed to get weirder and worse.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:59.030
Even though Daenerys begs Jon not to tell
his sisters about his real parentage, Jon

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:03.580
can't help himself, swearing both Arya and
Sansa to secrecy as he spills the beans about

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:04.890
his royal blood.

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:09.390
Despite her vow, Sansa quickly tells her former
husband Tyrion about who Jon really is, and

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:12.700
naturally, he immediately tells the secret
Varys.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:17.580
With information this important, it was always
impossible that characters wouldn't find out.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:21.470
But this turn of events is bad news for both
Jon and Daenerys, who both stand to lose a

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:24.510
lot the minute the truth of his lineage truly
goes public.

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:26.180
Score two for the Lions

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:29.930
Despite the recent victory against the Army
of the Dead, Daenerys is more on edge than

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:34.710
ever, even during the post-battle celebration
at Winterfell, where she finds herself isolated

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:39.240
from the crowd and left to wander off alone,
seemingly angry at her failure to make friends

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:40.380
among the Northerners.

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:44.790
By the end of the episode, Daenerys has faced
two massive losses, both pushing her to her

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:46.510
absolute breaking point.

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:50.880
Not only does she lose ships and cavalry during
a surprise attack on her fleet courtesy of

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:55.730
Euron Greyjoy and Cersei Lannister's army,
she loses her Rhaegal, who becomes the first

00:03:55.730 --> 00:04:00.570
of her dragons to be killed by humans with
the aid of massive ballistas known as scorpions.

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:04.610
In the aftermath, her best friend and confidante
Missandei ends up captured by the enemy, and

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:09.090
when Daenerys and her team offer Cersei her
life in exchange for her surrender, Cersei

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:13.550
has Missandei beheaded in front of them, another
cruel show of power from a monarch who knows

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:15.350
how to prove a brutal point.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:20.019
After losing Jorah, Rhaegal, and Missandei
in quick succession, Daenerys might be on

00:04:20.019 --> 00:04:23.080
the brink of succumbing to the madness that
runs in her family.

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:27.379
Even though Daenerys constantly says she wants
to avoid becoming her father, the "Mad King,"

00:04:27.379 --> 00:04:31.770
these tragedies all point to her reaching
a breaking point before long, especially as

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:34.910
this war continues to push her to her limit.

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:38.150
Meanwhile, Cersei has long been one of the
most brutal characters on the show, and despite

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:42.449
Tyrion's pleas for humanity and peace, she's
not changing anytime soon.

00:04:42.449 --> 00:04:46.300
For the moment, it appears that her ruthless
streak is still serving her well against her

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:48.300
more nobly intentioned enemies.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:51.970
Will her commitment to cruelty be the difference
maker in the coming war against Daenerys?

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:53.880
Or will it be her undoing?

